# M1-539 golden-path smoke scenario (live-e2e Phase 4a).
#
# Bootstrap-admin-only and DM-centric: it needs no DB seeding and no dynamic
# value chaining, so the same steps run green on a fresh inmemory deployment in
# CI and — via a later ConversationBackend binding — on a real SimpleX transport
# in Phase 4b. It proves the RUNNER (ordered send->expect steps, both match
# kinds, per-step latency capture), not lifecycle correctness, which stays in
# GoldenPathJourneyIT and the per-scenario ITs (D-live-5).
#
# Grammar (see Scenario.java):
#   send dm    <contactId> <text...>
#   send group <groupId> <senderContactId> <text...>
#   expect substring <timeoutMs> <literal text...>
#   expect regex     <timeoutMs> <java regex...>
#
# The admin contact id below must match infochat.adapters.inmemory.admin in the
# running deployment / test profile.

# 1. The bootstrap admin lists commands -> proves DM send + reply on the sent
#    channel, matched by a stable header substring.
send dm scn-smoke-admin /help
expect substring 5000 Available commands:

# 2. The admin mints a targeted single-use invite -> proves a second ordered step
#    matched by regex against the minted code (a UUID), a token that cannot rot
#    the way localized reply prose can.
send dm scn-smoke-admin /invite create --adapter inmemory --contact scn-smoke-invitee
expect regex 5000 [0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}
